  <content>
  <section>
    <section class="check-understanding">
      <exercise data-content-id="b491d30f-059b-4964-a89b-9781c582952c">
        <problem>
          <para>
      <para>Translate to an equation: Which equation means nine more than x is equal to 52?</para>
      </para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para>\(x+9=52\)</para>
          <para>\(9x=52\)</para>
          <para>\(9-x=52\)</para>
          <para>\(\frac{52}x=9\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>\(x+9=52\)</para>
          <para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(x\) + 9 = 52. </para>
      <para>Nine more than \(x\) means that 9 is added to \(x\).
        \(x+9\)
        Equal to 52 means that we take whatever expression that is in front of 52 and set them equal to each other.
        \(x+9=52\)</para>
    </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </section>
